Finally, to generate synthetic X-rays, the reposed 3D meshes must be converted back into a dense 3D volume.  Voxelization: Convert the reposed meshes back into a 3D grid.Hounsfield Unit (HU) Mapping: Assign the original CT HU values back to the repositioned bones and organs.  Soft Tissue Fill: Fill the residual space inside the newly posed SMPL body envelope with a constant mean HU value derived from the patient's original muscle tissue.  Ray Tracing: Pass this new volume into a framework like DeepDRR to simulate X-ray projections through the reposed anatomy.  
